  "has_voiceover": false,
  "description": "Its been a while...lets test one out...",
  "body_html": "<p>We have already talked about this stock a few times, I’ll link the posts below. We began cutting positions late September…and what have we noticed with our few remaining positions? They aren’t working to well ☹️. If the strategy is not working…stop doing it! Besides that fact, this popular stock which has been declining and had a large breakout to the downside after their earnings came out lackluster. </p><p>The last short we did was Nvidia back in February, making 16.9% (I honestly cant wait to short that pig again! 🐖)</p><p>Some critical notes before proceeding forward:</p><ul><li><p>If you have never shorted before: START SMALL. You need to learn the buttons of your brokerage. There will be others at some point. </p></li><li><p>If you do not know how to short, go to google and type “how to short on (insert your brokerage).” While you are at it, also search “how to set a stop for a short position on (insert your brokerage).” Everyone’s brokerage is going to be different. </p></li><li><p><em><strong>Stops are not an option</strong></em>. Personally I use 1x margin to give myself essentially the same breathing room as I do a position in a cash account. Do not be lured in by the heavy leverage. <strong>You MUST have a game plan before proceeding.</strong> I have never had a margin call or a liquidation event. Do not come crying to me if you do not manage your position. You have been warned. </p></li><li><p>We do not HODL these. The goal is to get into a winning position relatively quickly, and snag profits. At least that is my approach. </p></li></ul><p>You do what is best for you. Yes, this trade could still go bad, just as a long position can. Anything is possible. But I think odds are in our favor. </p><p>The popular stock to short is: </p>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
